# Eluge, the Shoreless Sea: "The first instant or sorcery spell you cast each turn costs {U} (or {1}) less to cast for each land
# you control with a flood counter on it" (CR 601.2f, 118.7). Turn 3: Eluge (Black Lotus and an Island) floods Bot1's Mountain.
# Turn 5: in Bot1's upkeep Bot2 casts Lightning Bolt at Bot1 - an opponent's spell, which uses up nothing of Bot1's. Bot1's first
# instant of the turn, Brainstorm, then costs nothing (no line pays for it: a spell left owing mana fails the script), and the
# second costs its full {U}, paid by an Island with nothing left over. Turn 6, Bot2's turn: "each turn" is any turn, so Bot1's
# Lightning Strike ({1}{R}) in Bot2's upkeep is the first of that turn, and with no {U} in its cost the {U} comes off its generic
# mana instead (CR 118.7c; the rulings): it costs {R}, which the flooded Mountain pays alone - every other land Bot1 has is
# tapped.

